On-device AI means AI (artificial intelligence) is used to process data directly on a device, like a smartphone or tablet. Unlike cloud-based AI, which requires connecting to an AI service, on-device AI lets the device itself handle the processing. This means the device can analyze and use data it already has, like in facial recognition or location tracking. It's about the device being the AI engine, not an external server. Examples include things like device-based security (like unlocking a device) or personalized recommendations. It's about the device's capabilities and how it uses AI in real-time.

